  "aws-architecture": {
    title: "AWS Architecture",
    subtitle: "Designing secure, resilient and scalable workloads on Amazon Web Services",
    summary:
      "AWS architecture is the design of cloud infrastructure using services such as VPC, subnets, route tables, EC2, Elastic Load Balancing, Auto Scaling, S3, RDS, IAM and CloudWatch. A production architecture must explain not only which services are present, but also how traffic enters the system, how application components communicate, where data is stored, how identities are controlled, and how the workload behaves during failures. This lesson follows a realistic multi-tier web application deployed across multiple Availability Zones.",
    objectives: [
