      {
        title: "4. Data, Object Storage and Database Architecture",
        explanation:
          "Application compute should be separated from durable data storage. Amazon S3 is object storage suited to static assets, uploads, backups, logs and data-lake workloads. Amazon RDS provides managed relational database capabilities, including automated backups and Multi-AZ deployment options. A Multi-AZ database deployment is designed for availability and failover; it should not be confused with a read-scaling architecture. Database subnet groups, security groups, encryption keys, backup retention and recovery objectives all contribute to the final design. Applications must handle database connection interruptions and reconnect safely after failover.",
        responsibilities: [
          "S3 bucket: durable object storage with access policies and lifecycle controls.",
          "RDS: managed relational database engine and operational capabilities.",
          "KMS: key management for supported encryption use cases.",
          "Secrets Manager: managed storage and rotation workflows for credentials.",
          "Backup policies: recovery points and retention aligned to business needs."
