        responsibilities: [
          "Classify workloads by business criticality, data sensitivity and recovery objectives.",
          "Map application dependencies before choosing a provider.",
          "Compare native service capabilities, regional availability and operational requirements.",
          "Record workload ownership and the reason for each placement decision."
        ],
        implementation: [
          "Create a workload inventory containing owner, provider, region, dependencies and data classification.",
          "Build a placement decision record covering latency, compliance, service fit, skills and cost.",
          "Use portable deployment packaging where it provides measurable value, but retain provider-native services when they offer a justified advantage.",
          "Define an exit and migration approach for workloads with material provider dependency."
        ],
        productionConsiderations: [
          "A second provider does not create resilience unless capacity, data, identity and recovery procedures are ready.",
          "Cross-provider traffic can increase latency, egress charges and operational complexity.",
          "Avoid placing tightly coupled application components in different clouds without testing dependency latency and failure behavior.",
          "Review provider concentration and critical service dependencies during architecture governance."
        ],
        failureModes: [
          "Workloads are distributed across providers without clear ownership.",
          "An application depends on a managed service that has no equivalent recovery design elsewhere.",
