        explanation: "Global traffic management provides the entry point for users accessing applications deployed in different cloud environments. DNS-based routing, latency policies, geographic policies and health-aware endpoint selection can direct users to suitable regions or providers. The DNS layer must account for caching, TTL values, health-check intervals, resolver behavior and the time required for clients to observe a routing change. A DNS health check only proves the specific endpoint test that it performs; it does not prove that the complete application workflow is healthy. Applications should expose meaningful health signals and fail safely when a target is unavailable.",
        responsibilities: [
          "Resolve application names to approved cloud endpoints.",
          "Apply health, geography, latency and policy-based routing decisions.",
          "Coordinate certificate and domain ownership across providers.",
          "Define failover behavior and communicate its expected timing."
        ],
        implementation: [
          "Create stable application DNS names and map them to provider-specific ingress endpoints.",
          "Configure health checks against meaningful application readiness paths.",
          "Set TTL values according to recovery needs and resolver behavior.",
          "Test endpoint withdrawal, recovery and client reconnection from representative networks."
        ],
        productionConsiderations: [
          "DNS caching means failover is not necessarily instantaneous.",
          "A healthy load balancer may still route to an unhealthy application dependency.",
          "TLS certificates, host headers, cookies and session state must remain valid after traffic moves.",
          "Use controlled traffic shifting before sending all users to a newly activated provider."
        ],
        failureModes: [
          "Health checks report success while critical application functions are failing.",
          "Stale DNS responses continue directing clients to an unavailable endpoint.",
          "The secondary provider lacks capacity for the redirected production traffic.",
          "Authentication or session dependencies prevent users from completing requests after failover."
