      {
        title: "Cross-Cloud Networking and Connectivity",
        explanation: "Applications in separate cloud providers communicate through carefully designed network paths. Connectivity may use site-to-site VPN, provider-supported private interconnects, transit architectures or secured public APIs. The correct choice depends on throughput, latency, availability, security and cost requirements. Each environment needs a deliberate IP addressing plan because overlapping CIDR ranges can make routing ambiguous and prevent direct connectivity. Routing advertisements, route priorities, firewalls, DNS forwarding, MTU settings and asymmetric paths must be considered together. Private connectivity reduces exposure to the public internet but does not replace encryption, identity checks or application authorization.",
        responsibilities: [
